# Copy to `.env` for local `wrangler dev`. In production set each as a secret:
# `wrangler secret put <NAME>`, or `wrangler deploy --secrets-file .env`.
#
# Per environment, wrangler loads `.env`, then `.env.local`, then — when you
# pass `--env <name>` — `.env.<name>` and `.env.<name>.local`, each overriding
# the last. So a staging deployment is `.env.staging`, not an edit to
# wrangler.jsonc. Everything but this example file is gitignored.
#
# One caveat: if a `.dev.vars` exists it wins outright and none of the above is
# read. This project uses `.env`; keep a single file so there is no question
# which one is live.
#
# Cloudflare API credentials for `npm run cf` are deliberately not here — they
# authenticate you, not the Worker. See `.cf.env.example`.

# One Ed25519 private JWK (a single line) signing every card this Worker serves
# and every push-notification callback JWT. MUST include a `kid`. Generate with
# `npm run keygen`.
#
# Only the matching PUBLIC key is ever exposed, at /.well-known/jwks.json — the
# private half never leaves the Worker.
#
# One key, not one per agent: the card lives at a well-known URI, which RFC 8615
# defines per-authority, so this origin serves one card and the gateway pins one
# key. The agents share this Worker and this file anyway, so per-agent keys never
# expressed a boundary that existed. What separates them is the tenant claim in
# the gateway's token, which core checks against the tenant each request names.
A2A_SIGNING_KEY=

# GATEWAY_ORIGINS: JSON array of trusted gateway origins, e.g.
# ["https://gateway.example.com"]. A property of this deployment, like the key.
# Not a traditional secret, but kept out of wrangler.jsonc so it can differ per
# environment with no code change.
GATEWAY_ORIGINS=

# ARC_API_KEY: API key for the ARC-AGI-3 game API (three.arcprize.org), issued
# from the ARC-AGI-3 web console. Required only by the arc-player agent
# (@loopingai/plugins/arc-agi declares it). Delete this line if you remove it.
ARC_API_KEY=

# There is no credential here for any agent's own model loop, deliberately.
#
# Every agent in this Worker — both coders included — runs its round loop on
# Workers AI through the `AI` binding, which Cloudflare authenticates for the
# Worker. There is no key to store and no key to rotate for that path, and no
# AI Gateway token either: the binding does not send one. If a gateway `401`
# ever appears it means Authenticated Gateway is switched on for the gateway
# named by `aiGatewayId` in src/config.ts — switch it off.
#
# The `CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN_*` entries at the bottom are not an exception to
# this: they authenticate the Claude Code CLI running inside claude-coder's
# container, not any loop in this Worker, and no container ever sees one.

# GITHUB_TOKEN: used by @loopingai/plugins/repo to clone, push a work branch and
# open the pull request. Needs `contents: write` and `pull-requests: write` on
# the repositories the coder is pointed at — a fine-grained PAT scoped to those
# repos is the right shape, not a classic token with org-wide access.
#
# Mint it from a dedicated GitHub account made for the agent, not a personal
# one — provisioned and scoped like a teammate. The agent acts for the whole
# team, not one operator, so its commits, PRs and access should be auditable
# as its own rather than blended into a person's.
#
# It never enters the container as a command argument, it is offered only to the
# hosts on the repo plugin's allowlist (github.com by default) — a clone URL
# pointing anywhere else is refused before git runs — and pull requests are
# opened from the Worker rather than the sandbox, so the container never holds a
# credential that can write to the repository through the API.
#
# Required by **both** coders: `coder` and `claude-coder` install the same repo
# plugin and clone the same way. Delete this line only if you remove both.
GITHUB_TOKEN=

# GITHUB_NAME / GITHUB_EMAIL: the git identity coder commits carry. Both are
# optional; left blank, they fall back to a generic `looping-coder` identity.
#
# Set GITHUB_EMAIL to the dedicated account's own address (its GitHub-issued
# noreply email, `ID+username@users.noreply.github.com`, if it has no other) —
# GitHub attributes a commit to whichever account verifies that address, so an
# arbitrary or personal one attributes the agent's commits to nobody, or to
# the wrong somebody. Set GITHUB_NAME only if `looping-coder` isn't the name
# you want those commits to carry.
#
# Same requirement as GITHUB_TOKEN above.
GITHUB_NAME=
GITHUB_EMAIL=

# CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN_1 / _2: the credential pool the claude-coder agent's
# egress gateway draws on, in priority order. Each is a `claude setup-token` OAuth
# credential — a Claude **subscription**, not an API key, because a subscription
# is refused for raw Messages API calls on every frontier model and accepted from
# the sanctioned Claude Code client.
#
# The gateway uses `_1` until Anthropic answers 429, then rotates to `_2`, then
# reports the reset time and stops. Rotating either secret works as you would
# expect: spent/rejected state is keyed on a fingerprint of the credential rather
# than on its position, so a freshly minted token is tried immediately instead of
# inheriting the state of the one it replaced.
#
# **Neither ever enters the container.** They are read only inside
# `ClaudeCoderWorkspaceDO`'s egress gateway, which swaps one into the outbound
# request on the Worker side of the boundary; the session itself launches with a
# placeholder. That is what keeps them out of reach of a cloned repository's
# `postinstall` and of any shell the model drives.
#
# Required only by the claude-coder agent. To run on one credential, drop `_2`
# here, from `secrets.required` in wrangler.jsonc, *and* from
# `src/agents/claude-coder/claude-code.ts` — a name declared and left unset is
# typed as a definite string that is undefined at runtime, and warns on every
# local run. Delete both lines if you remove the agent.
#
# Note the caveat: these are deployment-wide, so one person's subscription backs
# everyone using this deployment. Fine for a single-operator fork; read Anthropic's
# terms before pointing a multi-tenant gateway at it.
CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN_1=
CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN_2=

# There is deliberately nothing else here. Everything the Worker reads is above;
# `wrangler.jsonc` holds the bindings, which are not secrets.
